(*
expect:
bell: struck 1
raw 0
bell: struck 5
bell: struck 8
finished
*)
(* ORDERING IS NOT A TYPO, and it is the same one 14_display/01 documents: the
   host leaf prints DURING the prim call, so `bell: struck 1` lands before the
   `raw 0` that reports that call's result.

   tuvm#94 stage 1 — the host half of the bell seam, exercised through BOTH
   halves on purpose. The raw `platform bellStrike:` forwarder is asserted first
   so the status code is observable at all (the Bell wrapper answers self, by
   design — a striking has no interesting result, only a failure mode), and then
   the wrapper strikes the two counts that matter on the bench: 5 is the odd
   count that exercises pairs plus a lone final stroke, 8 is the full
   end-of-watch. The host cannot make a sound, so what it owes this test is
   evidence that the seam was reached WITH THE COUNT THE NODE MEANT — which is
   exactly the thing a wrong-argument bug would break and a status code would
   not catch. *)
class BellStrike packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | bell |
    ('raw ' , (platform bellStrike: 1) printString) out.
    bell:: platform bell.
    bell strike: 5.
    bell strike: 8.
    'finished' out.
  )
) : (
)
